    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prom}"
      },
      "description": "Cumulative Layout Shift \u2014 shown as a MEAN, not a quantile. CLS is a unitless ratio in roughly 0\u20130.25, but the SDK gives every histogram the same default millisecond-scale buckets (0, 5, 10, 25 \u2026 10000), so every CLS observation lands in the first bucket and histogram_quantile() would return noise. The mean from _sum/_count is the only honest number available. Good < 0.1, poor > 0.25. Cumulative since the server started, so it only ratchets upward \u2014 one slow cold start pins it for the life of the process. Colour is deliberately neutral here; 'Share rated good' is the signal that recovers.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "text"
          },
          "decimals": 3,
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "no data yet",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 6,
